\section*{Patent Claims}

\subsection*{Claim 1 (Independent System Claim)}
A high-performance computational physics system for real-time relativistic
spacetime evolution, comprising:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item a block-structured adaptive mesh refinement (AMR) manifold configured
    to dynamically refine spatial regions according to curvature thresholds
    associated with apparent horizon formation;

    \item a $3+1$ BSSN metric evolution core executing numerical updates of the
    spacetime metric, extrinsic curvature, and gauge fields across the AMR
    hierarchy;

    \item a GPU-resident boundary-update subsystem comprising elementwise CUDA
    kernels configured to perform refinement, derefinement, and inter-level flux
    synchronization without CPU-side control;

    \item a constraint-verification module configured to compute ADM Hamiltonian
    and momentum constraint norms and enforce bounded stability conditions during
    evolution;

    \item a multi-messenger telemetry ingestion interface configured to receive
    external astrophysical data streams and cryptographically encapsulate said
    streams using lattice-based post-quantum encryption; and

    \item a sovereign homeostasis controller configured to maintain numerical
    stability across multiple physical regimes by adjusting refinement criteria,
    gauge conditions, and evolution parameters based on constraint-violation
    feedback.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Claim 2 (Independent Method Claim)}
A method for performing secure relativistic spacetime simulation, comprising:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item ingesting astrophysical telemetry and encapsulating the telemetry
    using a lattice-based post-quantum cryptographic scheme;

    \item mapping the telemetry into initial or boundary conditions on a
    discretized spacetime manifold;

    \item evolving the manifold using a BSSN $3+1$ formulation across a
    block-structured AMR hierarchy;

    \item executing refinement-boundary operations using GPU-resident
    elementwise kernels;

    \item detecting apparent horizon formation by evaluating null-expansion
    criteria;

    \item computing ADM constraint norms and enforcing bounded stability
    conditions; and

    \item adjusting evolution parameters in response to constraint-violation
    feedback to maintain multi-regime numerical homeostasis.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Claim 3 (Independent Medium Claim)}
A non-transitory computer-readable medium storing instructions that, when
executed by one or more processors, cause the processors to perform the method
of any of the preceding claims, including GPU-resident execution of AMR boundary
updates and cryptographically secure ingestion of multi-messenger telemetry.

